* Authorities of IyziTrace's IBM MQ metrics container, for one queue manager.
* Run on each queue manager as an MQ administrator:
*   runmqsc QMNAME < monitor-authorities.mqsc
* The operating-system group iyzmon, and a user in it, must exist on the queue manager's host first
* (docs/07-ibm-mq.md, step 1). Nothing here allows reading, putting or removing an application's
* messages.
*
* Besides DISPLAY commands, the container resets every queue's statistics (RESET QSTATS) and reads
* the queue manager's event queues, which removes the events it reads. Another tool that reads the
* same statistics or events gets only part of them.

* Connect, and read the queue manager's attributes and status.
SET AUTHREC OBJTYPE(QMGR) GROUP('iyzmon') AUTHADD(CONNECT, INQ, DSP)

* Send commands to the command server (PCF) and receive the answers on a temporary queue made from
* the model queue. A queue's own profile replaces '**' below, so it repeats CHG for RESET QSTATS.
SET AUTHREC PROFILE('SYSTEM.ADMIN.COMMAND.QUEUE') OBJTYPE(QUEUE) GROUP('iyzmon') AUTHADD(PUT, INQ, DSP, CHG)
SET AUTHREC PROFILE('SYSTEM.DEFAULT.MODEL.QUEUE') OBJTYPE(QUEUE) GROUP('iyzmon') AUTHADD(GET, INQ, DSP)

* Status of every queue (depth, oldest message, time on queue). RESET QSTATS needs chg, and IBM MQ
* has no narrower authority for it; chg also allows changing a queue's attributes. The queue manager
* still refuses it on SYSTEM.AUTH.DATA.QUEUE, which only mqm may use: one AMQ8077W per round.
SET AUTHREC PROFILE('**') OBJTYPE(QUEUE) GROUP('iyzmon') AUTHADD(INQ, DSP, CHG)

* The event queues the container reads, with CHG again for RESET QSTATS.
SET AUTHREC PROFILE('SYSTEM.ADMIN.CONFIG.EVENT') OBJTYPE(QUEUE) GROUP('iyzmon') AUTHADD(GET, BROWSE, INQ, DSP, CHG)
SET AUTHREC PROFILE('SYSTEM.ADMIN.PERFM.EVENT') OBJTYPE(QUEUE) GROUP('iyzmon') AUTHADD(GET, BROWSE, INQ, DSP, CHG)
SET AUTHREC PROFILE('SYSTEM.ADMIN.QMGR.EVENT') OBJTYPE(QUEUE) GROUP('iyzmon') AUTHADD(GET, BROWSE, INQ, DSP, CHG)

* Status of every channel. Client-connection channels are a separate object type; without this,
* every channel inquiry logs AMQ8245W for them.
SET AUTHREC PROFILE('**') OBJTYPE(CHANNEL) GROUP('iyzmon') AUTHADD(DSP)
SET AUTHREC PROFILE('**') OBJTYPE(CLNTCONN) GROUP('iyzmon') AUTHADD(DSP)
